---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Taxes & Fiscal Policy | Phil Burney for Commissioner"
  description="Phil Burney's platform on taxes and fiscal accountability for Rutherford County District 5."
>
  <section class="section platform-hero">
    <p class="tag">Platform</p>
    <h1>Taxes &amp; Fiscal Policy</h1>
    <p class="muted lead">
      Your tax dollars belong to you. Phil will fight for a county budget that is
      transparent, disciplined, and focused on services that residents actually use —
      not bloated administration and backroom spending.
    </p>
    <a href="/platform" class="btn btn-outline back-link">← All Platform Issues</a>
  </section>

  <section class="section platform-stack">
    <article class="card">
      <h2>Property Tax Fairness</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Rutherford County homeowners are shouldering a growing share of the tax burden.
        Phil believes that growth should pay for growth — meaning new development must
        bring the infrastructure funding it requires rather than pushing costs onto
        existing residents.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Require developer impact fees that reflect true infrastructure costs</li>
        <li>Oppose unfunded mandates that force property tax increases</li>
        <li>Review and reform tax incentive deals that benefit large corporations at residents' expense</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h2>Budget Transparency</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Residents deserve to know exactly where their money goes. Phil will push for
        open, readable budgets published online — not buried in PDF files no one can
        navigate.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Publish a plain-language county budget summary each year</li>
        <li>Post all contracts and expenditures above $10,000 online</li>
        <li>Hold regular town halls on budget priorities before votes are taken</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h2>Spending Accountability</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Every program funded by taxpayers should have measurable goals and be evaluated
        against them. Phil will push for outcome-based budgeting that rewards results
        and cuts what doesn't work.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Require annual performance reviews for county departments</li>
        <li>Eliminate redundant programs and administrative overlap</li>
        <li>Benchmark county costs against comparable North Carolina counties</li>
      </ul>
    </article>

    <article class="card">
      <h2>Fiscal Reserves &amp; Long-Term Planning</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        Good government plans ahead. Phil will advocate for maintaining healthy reserves,
        avoiding debt-financed operating expenses, and building a long-term capital plan
        that keeps taxes predictable.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Maintain county reserve funds at or above state-recommended levels</li>
        <li>Require multi-year fiscal projections with every major spending commitment</li>
        <li>Oppose using one-time funds for recurring expenses</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="cta-inner">
      <h2>Help shape the agenda</h2>
      <p>Phil wants to hear from taxpayers and small business owners in District 5.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/donations" class="btn btn-primary">Support the Campaign</a>
        <a href="/platform" class="btn btn-outline-light">View All Issues</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .platform-hero {
    padding-top: 3rem;
  }

  .platform-hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--brand);
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    max-width: 680px;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .back-link {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 1.1rem;
  }
</style>
